    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Blood Brothers is a 1995 documentary video that captures Bruce Springsteen’s reunion with the E Street Band during the sessions for Greatest Hits, offering a rare behind-the-scenes look at the group’s chemistry after several years apart. Issued through Columbia Music Video, it presents the band’s work in an intimate, celebratory light and focuses less on a traditional concert format than on the story of the reunion itself.\n\nThe film is especially significant for Springsteen fans because it documents a key transitional moment in his career: the first sustained collaboration with the E Street Band since the mid-1980s. Its mix of rehearsal footage, interview material, and performance highlights gives it lasting value as both a historical record and a tribute to one of rock’s most durable partnerships, and it was notable enough to earn a Grammy nomination for long-form music video.",
